Blocked on a real gap in util-linux, not in librsvg itself. gio-sys's
build.rs resolves gio-2.0.pc through pkg-config, whose `Requires:` chain
needs mount.pc (libmount) - util-linux ships the actual libmount.so fine
(dwm/blkid-dependent packages install cleanly) but does not install
libmount.pc/libblkid.pc/libuuid.pc at all. The older util-linux-libs
package did carry them, but util-linux's own recipe supersedes it
(same libuuid.so etc - installing both conflicts, "file conflict:
/usr/lib/libuuid.so is owned by util-linux") without carrying the .pc
files forward.

Confirmed reproducible: a fresh chroot with cairo, pango, gdk-pixbuf,
libxml2, pkgconf, xorgproto, libx11/libxrender/libxft/libxext/libxcb all
installed (everything else pango/cairo's own .pc Requires: chains ask
for) still fails identically - `pkg-config --libs gio-2.0` reports
"Package 'mount', required by 'gio-2.0', not found" with no other errors
once xorgproto and the X11 libs are present.

Fix belongs in util-linux's own recipe (install the .pc files its build
already produces, the way it already installs the .so files), not here -
not attempted this pass. Once that exists, `scraps add -s librsvg` with the
makedepend list above should be enough; nothing else was still failing
when this was left off.
